The cheapest fix in the book. Take your trained model;
          re-compute the running mean / variance of every BatchNorm
          layer using a few hundred unlabelled target images;
          freeze the affine $\gamma, \beta$. Done in 30 seconds, no
          back-prop. Often closes 30-60% of the gap when shift is
          mostly low-level (illumination, sensor noise).
